Known non-deterministic flake (same one already skipped for z3-4.14.1 and
z3-4.16.0.linux/.windows): z3-5.1.0's response to an unsupported
get-info/set-info key is sometimes a clean "unsupported", sometimes a
garbled raw help-text dump ("; Suppported get-info parameters: ...") that
jSMTLIB can't parse -- the exact shape differs between runs, and even
between the two Linux architectures within the same CI run. A .bad golden
(exact-match) can never stay in sync with genuinely non-deterministic
output. Observed on ubuntu-24.04-arm in CI; also now observed on
macos-14 (arm64) in a later run (see the separate z3-5.1.0.macos-arm64
skip), so this is not actually Linux-exclusive -- just not yet caught
on x86_64 macOS or on ubuntu-24.04 (non-arm) for this exact version.
